      "message": "These lines were the cause of the incremental build issues with the original CL due to multiple bugs.  Incorrect over-escaping was causing it to write to \".d\", because output was $2 but escaped inside \u0027\u0027, so it didn\u0027t expand until the inner bash -c that had an empty $2.  In addition the depsfile content written to the incorrect location was bogus.\n\nI\u0027m going to fix this by making the generated scripts always assume their input is $1 and their output is $2, instead of passing those in as arguments, and then using cat \u003e $2.d \u003c\u003c\u0027EOF\u0027 to write the depsfile.",
